1001	     * characters of the SHA-256 digest of {@code "<normalizedLastName>|<postcode>"}, where the last
1002	     * name is normalized for comparison (trimmed, internal whitespace collapsed, lower-cased) and the
1003	     * postcode is the already-validated 4-digit value. Because it is a pure function of the last name
1004	     * and postcode, any two owners sharing those - regardless of creation order or whether they opted
1005	     * into {@code sharesHousehold} - land in the same household automatically. Returns {@code null}
1006	     * when the owner has no postcode, so such owners belong to no household. This single value feeds
1007	     * both the duplicate detection ({@link #rejectDuplicate}) and the household-size count
1008	     * ({@link #assignHouseholdMembership}).
1009	     */
1010	    private String computeHouseholdId(OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto) {
1011	        String postcode = ownerFieldsDto.getPostcode();
1012	        if (postcode == null || postcode.isBlank()) {
1013	            return null;
1014	        }
1015	        String lastName = normalizeForComparison(ownerFieldsDto.getLastName());
1016	        return shaHexUpper(lastName + "|" + postcode, 12);
1017	    }
